# Positions `bitter` defines when it links a program, the way a linker
# defines symbols like `_end`. Import them like any other `pub` label:
#
#   from std.bitter.link import image_start, image_end
#
# and `bitter` resolves them against the whole linked image:
#
#   image_start   the first entry of the image
#   image_end     just past its last entry
#
# so `span(image_start, image_end)` is the image's size in bytes, and
# `span(image_start, label)` is `label`'s offset into it — what an
# executable header needs, however many files the program spans.
#
# The labels below only give importers something to name: this file is
# never compiled as part of a program, and their positions here mean
# nothing.

pub image_start:
pub image_end:
